{"id":"msg-481","timestamp":"2026-06-21T01:15:00+02:00","from":"agency-lead-developer","to":"agency-architect","phase":"ARCHITECTURE","type":"INFO","ref_doc":"03_architecture.md","message":"The client has rejected the previous architectural specification for lacking detail and implementation specifics. We must rewrite it from scratch. Please refer to the extensive research in 00_client_intel.md to provide the extreme level of granularity, technical precision, and skill documentation demanded. Start ONLY with drafting Task 1. Ensure you include exactly how it will work, required skills, and all implementation details. Do not draft the entire architecture in one go. Submit Task 1 for my validation before proceeding.","in_reply_to":"msg-480","status":"RESOLVED","devio_validation_key":"z9y8x7w6v5u4t3s2r1q0p"}
{"id":"msg-482","timestamp":"2026-06-21T01:16:00+02:00","from":"agency-architect","to":"agency-lead-developer","phase":"ARCHITECTURE","type":"SUBMIT","ref_doc":"03_architecture.md","message":"I have rewritten the architectural specification from scratch, beginning strictly with Task 1 as requested. Task 1 now includes extreme granularity, explicitly defining how the Custom State Machine will work, the exact TypeScript/VS Code API implementation details (Deep Modules, TDD, File System Watcher), and the required skill constraints. Please validate Task 1 before we proceed to any subsequent tasks.","in_reply_to":"msg-481","status":"RESOLVED","devio_validation_key":"7hfhg62x9823gbg9xdzlu","files":[{"path":"/home/viet/git-perso/MaxApp/Devio/agency_workspace/03_architecture.md","content":"# Architecture Specification: Devio Plugin Complete Revamp\n\n## System Overview\nThe Devio Plugin is being completely revamped to transition from a monolithic, horizontal feature architecture to a structured, vertical, task-oriented workflow based on State-of-the-Art multi-agent systems research. The Orchestration Engine will act as a central router (specifically, the Lead Developer persona acting as the Orchestrator), managing deterministic state transitions through an `inbox.jsonl` message bus. The architecture mandates the use of deep modules, explicit path linking for skill execution, and dynamic context injection using IDE-native `@path` resolution.\n\n## Architecture Diagram\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    Client[Client UI/VS Code] -->|Interacts| CEO[CEO Agent]\n    CEO -->|Proposal/Requirements| LeadDev[Lead Developer / Orchestrator]\n    \n    LeadDev -->|Tasks| Developer[Developer Agent]\n    LeadDev -->|Validates Architecture| Architect[Architect Agent]\n    LeadDev -->|Requests Intel| Researcher[Researcher Agent]\n    Developer -->|Testing/Review| QA[QA Agent]\n    \n    subgraph \"Devio Orchestration Engine (Custom State Machine)\"\n        MessageBus[(inbox.jsonl)]\n        StateManager[State Transitions]\n    end\n    \n    LeadDev <--> MessageBus\n    Developer <--> MessageBus\n    Architect <--> MessageBus\n    QA <--> MessageBus\n    Researcher <--> MessageBus\n    CEO <--> MessageBus\n```\n\n## Component Breakdown\n\n1. **Custom State Machine Orchestrator**\n   - **Purpose:** Governs the agency's lifecycle phases (Brief, Proposal, Architecture, Development, Review, Delivery, Done) and explicitly prevents agents from skipping steps.\n   - **Technology:** TypeScript (Native VS Code Extension).\n   - **Rationale:** A custom FSM is chosen over graph libraries (like LangGraph) to ensure predictable, deterministic step-by-step executions without introducing massive dependency bloat to the IDE plugin.\n\n2. **Event-Driven Message Bus (`inbox.jsonl`)**\n   - **Purpose:** Serves as the shared \"Blackboard\" where agents read and write state transitions and deliverables.\n   - **Technology:** JSONL file monitored via `vscode.workspace.createFileSystemWatcher`.\n   - **Rationale:** Native VS Code file system watchers provide a lightweight, dependency-free mechanism for real-time state synchronization across the React webview and backend.\n\n3. **Dynamic Context Injector**\n   - **Purpose:** Dynamically references fragmented Markdown skills to be injected into the agent prompt context.\n   - **Technology:** String appending of `@path` syntax in `prompt-builder.ts` leveraging Antigravity IDE native interception.\n   - **Rationale:** By simply appending `Context: @absolute_path`, the Antigravity IDE natively intercepts and embeds file content into the LLM context, bypassing complex file retrieval logic and CDP uploads within the plugin.\n\n## API Contract\n\n```typescript\n// Custom State Machine Interface\ninterface StateTransition {\n    fromPhase: string;\n    toPhase: string;\n    trigger: 'SUBMIT' | 'APPROVE' | 'REQUEST_CHANGE' | 'ESCALATE';\n    actor: string; // The agent executing the transition\n}\n\n// Message Bus Event\ninterface MessageBusEvent {\n    id: string;\n    timestamp: string;\n    from: string;\n    to: string;\n    phase: string;\n    type: string;\n    ref_doc: string | null;\n    message: string;\n    status: 'OPEN' | 'RESOLVED';\n}\n```\n\n## Data Model\n\n| Entity | Attributes | Relationships |\n|:---|:---|:---|\n| Message | id, timestamp, from, to, phase, type, message, ref_doc, status | One-to-Many with State Transitions |\n| Workspace State | currentPhase, activeAgent, pendingTasks | Updated by Orchestrator based on Messages |\n\n## Infrastructure & Deployment\n- **Environment:** Runs purely as a VS Code extension inside the user's IDE.\n- **Deployment:** Packaged as a `.vsix` file using VS Code Extension tooling (`vsce`).\n- **Cloud Costs:** €0.00 (Local execution, relying on client-provided LLM endpoints).\n\n## Implementation Task List\n\n> **CRITICAL WORKFLOW RULE:** Tasks are executed strictly one-by-one. We will not proceed to the next task until the current task is completed, validated, and approved. No subsequent tasks will be drafted until Task 1 is validated.\n\n### Task 1: Core Custom State Machine & Event-Driven Engine Bootstrapping\n- **Estimated Hours:** 16 hours\n- **Dependencies:** None\n- **Role Requirement:** Developer Agent (Strictly governed by Lead Developer)\n- **Technical Context & SOTA Reference:** SOTA Research - Global Orchestration & Workflow (Explicit FSM over Prompt Chaining) & Professional Coding Standards.\n\n**Detailed Functional Description:**\nImplement the foundational lightweight, custom Finite State Machine (FSM) in the orchestration engine. This code must be written in TypeScript natively within the VS Code extension. The engine must enforce deterministic, vertical task execution by rigorously governing the Devio agency's core lifecycle phases: `Brief`, `Proposal`, `Architecture`, `Development`, `Review`, `Delivery`, and `Done`. The FSM must explicitly reject any attempt by an agent to bypass sequential requirements (e.g., jumping from Proposal to Development without Architecture approval).\n\n**Granular Implementation Details:**\n1. **Directory Structure & Ubiquitous Language:** Create an isolated domain model representing the state machine. Use strictly defined TypeScript enums for `PhaseState` and `TransitionEvent` to precisely mirror the architectural definitions. Do not use generic string states.\n2. **State Evaluation Loop:** Implement `OrchestrationEngine.ts` utilizing John Ousterhout's \"Deep Modules\" principle. The state transition logic must be fully isolated from any file system I/O. The engine must evaluate transitions solely triggered by explicit, validated message types (`SUBMIT`, `APPROVE`, `REQUEST_CHANGE`, `ESCALATE`) arriving on the bus.\n3. **Message Bus Integration:** Integrate directly with the JSONL parser reading `agency_workspace/inbox.jsonl`.\n4. **File System Watcher Hook:** Hook the FSM evaluations to the `vscode.workspace.createFileSystemWatcher` event specifically watching `inbox.jsonl`. When an append is detected, the event loop must parse the new line and determine if a valid state transition applies based on the current phase and the actor roles.\n\n**Skill Requirements (Agent Constraints):**\n- **Lead Developer Orchestration:** The Lead Developer must be programmed as the central Orchestrator in this topology. The FSM must reject state transitions initiated by unauthorized personas (e.g., a Developer approving an Architecture phase).\n- **TDD Compliance:** The developer must write tests *before* the functional code.\n- **Dependency Minimization:** Do not use any third-party state machine libraries (like XState). Rely entirely on native TS classes/enums.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- `OrchestrationEngine.ts` is implemented using deep modules, isolating state transition logic from file system I/O.\n- Strict enums for `PhaseState` and `TransitionEvent` are implemented.\n- A comprehensive TDD test suite (100% coverage on transition logic) verifies that the FSM explicitly rejects invalid phase transitions and correctly advances the state phase when an `APPROVE` message from a valid reviewer is detected.\n- The `vscode.workspace.createFileSystemWatcher` correctly triggers the FSM evaluation loop upon `inbox.jsonl` appends without crashing or infinite looping.\n"}]}
