{"id": "msg-503", "timestamp": "2026-06-20T23:50:43.023202Z", "from": "agency-architect", "to": "agency-lead-developer", "phase": "ARCHITECTURE", "type": "SUBMIT", "ref_doc": "03_architecture.md", "message": "I have drafted ONLY the first segment of the architectural roadmap in 03_architecture.md as requested. It now explicitly details the System Overview (including the UI/UX interaction model) and Phase 1: the complete Agent list along with their specific lifecycle phases, responsibilities, and exact Skill Mappings. Please review and validate this segment before I proceed to draft the elaboration of the complete step-by-step process.", "in_reply_to": "msg-502", "status": "RESOLVED", "devio_validation_key": "c8x9e2m4n5b1v3c0z7l8k", "files": [{"path": "/home/viet/git-perso/MaxApp/Devio/agency_workspace/03_architecture.md", "content": "# Architecture Specification: Devio Plugin Complete Revamp\n\n## System Overview & UX Interaction Model\nThe Devio Plugin is being completely revamped to transition from a monolithic, horizontal feature architecture to a structured, vertical, task-oriented workflow based on State-of-the-Art multi-agent systems research. \n\nFrom a user experience (UX) perspective, the human interacts with the plugin through a React-based webview and chat panel. The user inputs requests which are routed to the CEO agent. The user has full visibility into the agentic workflow: they can see state transitions, agent outputs, and explicit validation requests within the chat panel. The Orchestration Engine acts as the central backend router, managing deterministic state transitions through an `inbox.jsonl` message bus. The architecture mandates the use of deep modules, explicit path linking for skill execution, and dynamic context injection using IDE-native `@path` resolution.\n\n## Phased Implementation Roadmap\n\n> **CRITICAL WORKFLOW RULE:** Tasks are executed strictly one-by-one. We will not proceed to the next task until the current task is completed, validated, and approved. No subsequent tasks will be drafted until the current segment is validated.\n\n### Phase 1: Complete Agent List and Explicit Skill Mappings\n\nThis phase details the complete roster of specialized agents within the Devio agency, including their specific lifecycle phases, responsibilities, and explicitly mapped skills (Markdown instruction sets).\n\n#### 1. agency-ceo\n- **Active Phases:** BRIEF, PROPOSAL, DELIVERY\n- **Responsibilities:** Interacts directly with the human user via the React webview. Gathers requirements, drafts business proposals, phased project roadmaps, and quotes. Manages the inbox for challenges from the Architect or QA, and compiles the final client delivery package.\n- **Explicit Skill Mappings:** `agency-ceo/SKILL.md`, `references/message_types.md`\n\n#### 2. agency-researcher\n- **Active Phases:** BRIEF\n- **Responsibilities:** Operates invisibly to the human user. Performs due diligence on the client based on initial requirements, searching for business context, and producing a client intelligence report (`00_client_intel.md`).\n- **Explicit Skill Mappings:** `agency-researcher/SKILL.md`\n\n#### 3. agency-lead-developer (Orchestrator)\n- **Active Phases:** PROPOSAL, ARCHITECTURE, DEVELOPMENT\n- **Responsibilities:** Acts as the Pragmatic Architect and Central Orchestrator. Enforces the strict task-by-task cooperational relay protocol. Translates client requirements into rigorously researched execution plans and validates architectural tasks before development begins.\n- **Explicit Skill Mappings:** `agency-lead-developer/SKILL.md`\n\n#### 4. agency-architect\n- **Active Phases:** ARCHITECTURE, REVIEW (escalation), PROPOSAL (review)\n- **Responsibilities:** Designs the full system architecture, defining the technical stack and ensuring scalability. Drafts the implementation task list strictly segment-by-segment for the Lead Developer's validation.\n- **Explicit Skill Mappings:** `agency-architect/SKILL.md`\n\n#### 5. agency-accountant\n- **Active Phases:** PROPOSAL, ARCHITECTURE\n- **Responsibilities:** Handles financial modeling, budget planning, and quote calculations. Ensures that the proposed architecture aligns with the client's financial constraints.\n- **Explicit Skill Mappings:** `agency-accountant/SKILL.md`\n\n#### 6. agency-designer\n- **Active Phases:** PROPOSAL, ARCHITECTURE, DEVELOPMENT\n- **Responsibilities:** Responsible for UI/UX visual style, layouts, and aesthetic presentation. Ensures the human-facing React webview and interactive elements meet professional design standards.\n- **Explicit Skill Mappings:** `agency-designer/SKILL.md`\n\n#### 7. agency-developer\n- **Active Phases:** DEVELOPMENT\n- **Responsibilities:** Reads the validated architecture specification and implements the solution. Writes code, creates files, logs progress, and responds to QA change requests with revisions.\n- **Explicit Skill Mappings:** `agency-developer/SKILL.md`\n\n#### 8. agency-qa\n- **Active Phases:** REVIEW, ARCHITECTURE (escalation)\n- **Responsibilities:** Reviews code for bugs, security vulnerabilities, and strict alignment with the architecture spec. Issues the final APPROVE to the Lead Developer.\n- **Explicit Skill Mappings:** `agency-qa/SKILL.md`\n\n#### 9. agency-trinity (HR & Analytics)\n- **Active Phases:** Post-Mortem, Escalation, Closing Sequence\n- **Responsibilities:** Uses native tools to read the message bus (`inbox.jsonl`), analyzes agency performance, and generates structured insights for the company and individual agents.\n- **Explicit Skill Mappings:** `agency-trinity/SKILL.md`\n\n#### 10. agency-secretary (Nyobe)\n- **Active Phases:** DONE\n- **Responsibilities:** Responsible for archiving workspace documents and managing state. Archives only after Trinity has completed her analysis.\n- **Explicit Skill Mappings:** `agency-secretary/SKILL.md`\n\n*(Next Segment: Elaboration of the complete step-by-step process... Pending Lead Developer Validation)*\n"}]}
